{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>But the soul that acts with a high hand, etc.</b> Meaning: one who serves idolatry deliberately — Scripture elevates this as though he blasphemed HaShem, heaven forfend, and therefore his punishment is ״הַנֶּפֶשׁ הַהִיא מִקֶּרֶב עַמָּהּ וְנִכְרְתָה״ (that soul shall be cut off from among its people)." "Further, it says <b>because the word of HaShem he has despised, etc.</b> — meaning, since it is weighed against the entire Torah, he has thereby nullified all positive commandments, which is what the verse means by ״דְבַר ה׳ בָּזָה״ (he despised the word of HaShem), and he has also transgressed all negative commandments, which is what it means by <b>and his commandment he has broken</b>. And therefore ״הִכָּרֵת תִּכָּרֵת הַנֶּפֶשׁ הַהִיא״ — הִכָּרֵת corresponds to the sinews of the soul, תִּכָּרֵת corresponds to its limbs, for the souls have 248 limbs and 365 sinews, corresponding to which HaShem gave 248 positive commandments and 365 negative commandments. When one transgresses them all, no branch remains from which it may live, and it has no revival anymore, and the sin becomes fixed in it forever and ever — and this is the meaning of ״<b>עֲוֹנָה בָהּ</b>״. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded the verse in a different sense (Sifrei, Sanhedrin 90b), for the Torah has seventy faces."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:49.479234225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}